  "Sunlight looks white but is a mixture of every colour. As it passes through the air, it is scattered in all directions by the gas molecules it meets, and shorter wavelengths are scattered far more strongly than longer ones. Blue light therefore reaches your eyes from every part of the sky. At sunset the light travels through much more air, most of the blue is scattered away, and what remains looks orange and red.",
